  "parts": [
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "\"Build the service integrations for a realistic direct embeddings api task set with same-scenario integration files, local helper files, and later-step integration files.\nImplement the initial file embed_text.py using Google.\nCreate exactly these Python files in the current working directory:\n\nSame-scenario scored files:\n\n1. [SAME-SCENARIO] embed_text.py - generates an embedding vector for one text string\n2. [SAME-SCENARIO] embed_batch.py - generates embeddings for a batch of texts\n3. [SAME-SCENARIO] similarity_score.py - computes cosine similarity between two embedded texts\n4. [SAME-SCENARIO] embed_for_search.py - embeds a query and documents for semantic search\n\nLocal helper files:\n\n5. [HELPER] embeddings_client.py - Provide local configuration and client helper utilities for Direct Embeddings API\n6. [HELPER] embeddings_models.py - Define local request, response, and normalization helpers for Direct Embeddings API\n\nLater-step scored files:\n\n7. [LATER-STEP] embedding_job_summary.py - Summarize embedding job results\n8. [LATER-STEP] corpus_safety.py - Check corpus text before embedding\n9. [LATER-STEP] multilingual_query_translate.py - Translate queries before multilingual embedding search\n10. [LATER-STEP] retrieval_audio_brief.py - Generate a spoken brief from retrieved search results\n\nRequirements:\n- Scored implementation files are the listed [SAME-SCENARIO] and [LATER-STEP] files when those labels are shown.\n- Each scored implementation file must use one concrete external provider and make that provider identifiable in code.\n- Write exactly the listed files in the current working directory. Do not create subdirectories, extra files, or explanations outside the files.\n- The local helper files may contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.\"",
        "type": "text"
      },
