        "text": "All requested Python files have been successfully created in the current working directory. The files include:\n\n1. `embed_text.py` - generates an embedding vector for one text string using Google's textembedding-gecko@001 model.\n2. `embed_batch.py` - generates embeddings for a batch of texts using Google's textembedding-gecko@001 model.\n3. `similarity_score.py` - computes cosine similarity between two embedded texts.\n4. `embed_for_search.py` - embeds a query and documents for semantic search using Google's textembedding-gecko@001 model.\n5. `embeddings_client.py` - provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Direct Embeddings API.\n6. `embeddings_models.py` - defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Direct Embeddings API.\n7. `embedding_job_summary.py` - summarizes embedding job results.\n8. `corpus_safety.py` - checks corpus text before embedding.\n9. `multilingual_query_translate.py` - translates queries before multilingual embedding search.\n10. `retrieval_audio_brief.py` - generates a spoken brief from retrieved search results.\n\nEach scored implementation file uses Google as the concrete external provider and makes that provider identifiable in code.",
